{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Knot.M004AngleStructure","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Knot.M004AngleStructure","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":30,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.M004AngleStructure.GA_on_line","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.M004AngleStructure.GA_on_line","kind":"theorem","line":214,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/M004AngleStructure.lean#L214-L218","doc":"The fixed line is genuinely inside the polytope: every `t ∈ (0, 1/2)` gives\na feasible positive point.  So the one-dimensionality in `fixed_iff_line` is a\nreal degree of freedom, not an empty set. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.M004AngleStructure.fixed_positive_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.M004AngleStructure.fixed_positive_iff","kind":"theorem","line":205,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/M004AngleStructure.lean#L205-L212","doc":"Positivity confines the fixed line to `0 < t < 1/2`; the regular point sits\nstrictly inside, so it is not a boundary artefact. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.M004AngleStructure.regular_unique_on_fixed_locus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.M004AngleStructure.regular_unique_on_fixed_locus","kind":"theorem","line":200,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/M004AngleStructure.lean#L200-L203","doc":"…and strictly so away from it — the maximiser is unique. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.M004AngleStructure.regular_maximises_on_fixed_locus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.M004AngleStructure.regular_maximises_on_fixed_locus","kind":"theorem","line":192,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/M004AngleStructure.lean#L192-L198","doc":"Restated as a maximisation: on the fixed line the regular point is the\nunique maximiser of the minimum angle. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.M004AngleStructure.minAngleOnLine_lt_of_ne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.M004AngleStructure.minAngleOnLine_lt_of_ne","kind":"theorem","line":178,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/M004AngleStructure.lean#L178-L190","doc":"**The Casson–Rivin objective is uniquely maximised at the regular point.**\nOff `t = 1/3` the minimum angle is strictly smaller — below it because `t`\nitself is, above it because `1 - 2t` is.\n\nThis is what replaces the bean's false hypothesis (ii): the symmetry cuts the\nfeasible set to a line, and the objective — not the symmetry — picks the point\non it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.M004AngleStructure.minAngleOnLine_regular","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.M004AngleStructure.minAngleOnLine_regular","kind":"theorem","line":175,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/M004AngleStructure.lean#L175-L176","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.M004AngleStructure.minAngleOnLine","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.M004AngleStructure.minAngleOnLine","kind":"def","line":171,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/M004AngleStructure.lean#L171-L173","doc":"The minimum angle at a point of the fixed line.  Every coordinate is `t` or\n`1 - 2t`, so the whole objective collapses to a two-term `min`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.M004AngleStructure.Fixed_regular","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.M004AngleStructure.Fixed_regular","kind":"theorem","line":165,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/M004AngleStructure.lean#L165-L167","doc":"The regular point is on the fixed line, at `t = 1/3`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.M004AngleStructure.Positive_regular","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.M004AngleStructure.Positive_regular","kind":"theorem","line":162,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/M004AngleStructure.lean#L162-L163","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.M004AngleStructure.GA_regular","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.M004AngleStructure.GA_regular","kind":"theorem","line":156,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/M004AngleStructure.lean#L156-L160","doc":"The regular point `(1/3, …, 1/3)` — two regular ideal tetrahedra — is\nfeasible. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.M004AngleStructure.fixed_iff_line","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.M004AngleStructure.fixed_iff_line","kind":"theorem","line":140,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/M004AngleStructure.lean#L140-L154","doc":"**The exact fixed locus of the symmetry group, as an `iff`.**\n\nA feasible point is fixed by both generators **iff** it lies on the line\n`(t, 1 − 2t, t, 1 − 2t, t, t)`.  Because this is an iff, it settles the bean's\nhypothesis (ii) NEGATIVELY: the fixed set is one-dimensional, so the symmetric\npoint is not unique and symmetry alone cannot pin the optimum. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.M004AngleStructure.Fixed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.M004AngleStructure.Fixed","kind":"def","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/M004AngleStructure.lean#L136-L138","doc":"Being fixed by both generators. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.M004AngleStructure.Positive.tau","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.M004AngleStructure.Positive.tau","kind":"theorem","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/M004AngleStructure.lean#L129-L132","doc":"Likewise for τ. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.M004AngleStructure.Positive.sigma","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.M004AngleStructure.Positive.sigma","kind":"theorem","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/M004AngleStructure.lean#L124-L127","doc":"Positivity is permutation-invariant, so it survives σ. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.M004AngleStructure.GA.tau","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.M004AngleStructure.GA.tau","kind":"theorem","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/M004AngleStructure.lean#L115-L122","doc":"**Generator τ**: `(α₁,β₁,γ₁,α₂,β₂,γ₂) ↦ (β₂,α₂,γ₂,β₁,α₁,γ₁)`.\nIt preserves `GA` by swapping BOTH the tetrahedra and the edge equations. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.M004AngleStructure.GA.sigma","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.M004AngleStructure.GA.sigma","kind":"theorem","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/M004AngleStructure.lean#L106-L113","doc":"**Generator σ**: `(α₁,β₁,γ₁,α₂,β₂,γ₂) ↦ (γ₁,β₁,α₁,α₂,γ₂,β₂)`.\nIt preserves `GA` by SWAPPING the two edge equations. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.M004AngleStructure.Positive.hγ₂","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.M004AngleStructure.Positive.hγ₂","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/M004AngleStructure.lean#L102-L102","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.M004AngleStructure.Positive.hβ₂","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.M004AngleStructure.Positive.hβ₂","kind":"theorem","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/M004AngleStructure.lean#L101-L101","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.M004AngleStructure.Positive.hα₂","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.M004AngleStructure.Positive.hα₂","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/M004AngleStructure.lean#L100-L100","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.M004AngleStructure.Positive.hγ₁","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.M004AngleStructure.Positive.hγ₁","kind":"theorem","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/M004AngleStructure.lean#L99-L99","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.M004AngleStructure.Positive.hβ₁","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.M004AngleStructure.Positive.hβ₁","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/M004AngleStructure.lean#L98-L98","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.M004AngleStructure.Positive.hα₁","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.M004AngleStructure.Positive.hα₁","kind":"theorem","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/M004AngleStructure.lean#L97-L97","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.M004AngleStructure.Positive.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.M004AngleStructure.Positive.mk","kind":"ctor","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/M004AngleStructure.lean#L96-L96","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.M004AngleStructure.Positive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.M004AngleStructure.Positive","kind":"structure","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/M004AngleStructure.lean#L95-L102","doc":"Strict positivity of all six angles — the open part of the polytope. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.M004AngleStructure.GA.edge₂","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.M004AngleStructure.GA.edge₂","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/M004AngleStructure.lean#L93-L93","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.M004AngleStructure.GA.edge₁","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.M004AngleStructure.GA.edge₁","kind":"theorem","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/M004AngleStructure.lean#L92-L92","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.M004AngleStructure.GA.tet₂","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.M004AngleStructure.GA.tet₂","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/M004AngleStructure.lean#L91-L91","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.M004AngleStructure.GA.tet₁","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.M004AngleStructure.GA.tet₁","kind":"theorem","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/M004AngleStructure.lean#L90-L90","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.M004AngleStructure.GA.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.M004AngleStructure.GA.mk","kind":"ctor","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/M004AngleStructure.lean#L89-L89","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.M004AngleStructure.GA","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.M004AngleStructure.GA","kind":"structure","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/M004AngleStructure.lean#L83-L93","doc":"**The m004 generalised angle structure**, in π-units, on the six tetrahedron\nangles `(α₁, β₁, γ₁, α₂, β₂, γ₂)`.\n\n`tet₁`/`tet₂` are the per-tetrahedron sums; `edge₁`/`edge₂` are SnapPy's two\nedge equations for m004. The four are rank 3 (the edge sum is twice the tet\nsum), matching the 3-dimensional solution space the LP was solved over. ","signatureChunk":0}]}